  "body": "The release where **one Mercury runtime serves every terminal you open.** `mercury attach` connects a second terminal to the running session — a full live TUI over the runtime's event feed — while the runtime itself keeps running untouched in the first.\n\n## Highlights\n\n### `mercury attach`\n- **Second terminal, same Mercury** — `mercury attach` connects to the already-running runtime and opens the full TUI: live streaming, step markers, prompts, input. The runtime is never touched from the attached side.\n- **Auto-attach** — a second `mercury` invocation finds the running runtime and attaches instead of starting a duplicate.\n- **Native scrollback** (same model as the main TUI) — finalized messages print once into the terminal's own scrollback through `<Static>`; only the small live region (streaming tail, steps, prompt, input, status) repaints.\n- **Every surface's history** — the conversation history comes from the shared session repository, so messages sent from other surfaces (CLI, Telegram, web) are visible as history in the attached view.\n- **Clean detach** — Ctrl+C detaches; the runtime keeps running (`mercury stop` stops it).\n\n### Attach-token auth\n- **Machine-local token** written at boot to `attach-token` (`0600` — same trust level as credential files), rotated on every restart.\n- **Loopback-only**: the token is accepted only from `127.0.0.1` connections — non-loopback or wrong token gets `401`.\n- Regular web session tokens still work for API calls unchanged.\n\n### Website & docs\n- New **Cloud Instance** platform guide — hosted Mercury via [Atomic Bot](https://atomicbot.ai)\n- New **completion architecture** reference page\n- Richer per-page OG preview cards with sections, description, and breadcrumb\n\n## Fixed\n- `perm-tui-repaint` test stabilized for CI: ink suppresses non-static frame writes under `is-in-ci` (only `<Static>` output survives); the test now clears `CI` before ink loads and polls for the rendered frame instead of sleeping\n- Windows: POSIX file-mode assertion skipped in `attach-token` test (Windows doesn't enforce `0600`; `stat` reports `0666` for writable files)"
}
